          {
            "title": "Lists and duplicates",
            "id": 89320,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Unlike sets, lists like <code>grocery_list</code> allow for duplicate values, like <code>\"broccoli\"</code> here.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"grocery_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;cereal&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;milk&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"16\" endIndex=\"26\" /><option startIndex=\"46\" endIndex=\"56\" /></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>\"broccoli\"</code>, followed by <code>\"broccoli\"</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Eliminate duplicates",
            "id": 89321,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>To eliminate duplicates from a list like <code>grocery_list</code>, we can transform it into a set with <code>set()</code>, and the list between parentheses.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"grocery_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;cereal&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;milk&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(set(grocery_list))\" /><text type=\"break\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"65\" endIndex=\"68\" /><option startIndex=\"68\" endIndex=\"69\" /><option startIndex=\"69\" endIndex=\"81\" /><option startIndex=\"81\" endIndex=\"82\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{'broccoli', 'milk', 'cereal'}\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>set</code> followed by <code>(</code> and then <code>grocery_list</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Store in variable",
            "id": 89322,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Used on a list, <code>set()</code> gives us a set of the unique list values, which we can then store in a variable like <code>grocery_set</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"grocery_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;cereal&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;milk&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"grocery_set = set(grocery_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(grocery_set)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"70\" /><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"73\" endIndex=\"90\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{'broccoli', 'milk', 'cereal'}\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>grocery_set</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>set(grocery_list)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Store the unique values from <code>grocery_list</code> in <code>grocery_set</code>, then display that set.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"grocery_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;cereal&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;milk&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;broccoli&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"grocery_set = set(grocery_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(grocery_set)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"59\" endIndex=\"70\" /><option startIndex=\"71\" endIndex=\"72\" /><option startIndex=\"73\" endIndex=\"90\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"list(grocery_list)\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"grocery_list\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>grocery_set</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, and finally <code>set(grocery_list)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Lists and duplicates",
            "id": 89417,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's the difference between sets and lists in terms of duplicate values?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Lists allow duplicates, while sets don't</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Sets allow duplicates, while lists don't</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Lists allow duplicates, while sets don't.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Lists allow duplicate values, while sets do not.</p><p>For <code>tags = [\"new\", \"sale\", \"new\"]</code>, how many values are in <code>tags</code> and <code>set(tags)</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">The list has <code>3</code> values and the set has <code>2</code>.</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Both collections have <code>3</code> values.</item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">The list has <code>2</code> values and the set has <code>3</code>.</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">The list has <code>3</code> values and the set has <code>2</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Eliminate duplicates",
            "id": 89418,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What's an easy way to eliminate duplicate values from a list?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">Converting the list into a set to discard the duplicates</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">Looping over the list to remove duplicates</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Converting the list into a set to discard the duplicates.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>An easy way to eliminate duplicates from a list is to convert it into a set.</p><p>You have <code>names = [\"Ana\", \"Bo\", \"Ana\"]</code>.</p><p>Which line stores the unique values from <code>names</code> in <code>unique_names</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\"><code>unique_names = set(names)</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\"><code>unique_names = names</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\"><code>names = set(unique_names)</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>unique_names = set(names)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Question: Store in variable",
            "id": 89419,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>What can we get from <code>set()</code>?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A set based on the collection of values between the parentheses</item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A list based on the set between the parentheses</item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A set based on the collection of values between the parentheses.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>The <code>set()</code> instruction creates a set from the collection between its parentheses.</p><p>What does <code>set([\"a\", \"a\", \"b\"])</code> produce?</p><selection iscode=\"false\" multiple=\"multiple\"><item value=\"1\" correct=\"true\">A set containing <code>\"a\"</code> and <code>\"b\"</code></item><item value=\"2\" correct=\"false\">A list containing <code>\"a\"</code> and <code>\"b\"</code></item><item value=\"3\" correct=\"false\">A set containing two separate <code>\"a\"</code> values and one <code>\"b\"</code></item></selection><p visible-if=\"wrong\">A set containing <code>\"a\"</code> and <code>\"b\"</code>.</p></body></html>"
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Eliminate duplicates",
            "id": 89421,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Eliminate duplicates from <code>drinks_list</code> using the <code>set()</code> instruction.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"drinks_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;espresso&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;americano&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(set(drinks_list))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"82\" endIndex=\"85\" /><option startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"86\" /><option startIndex=\"86\" endIndex=\"97\" /><option startIndex=\"97\" endIndex=\"98\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{'chai', 'americano', 'espresso', 'matcha'}\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>set</code> followed by <code>(</code> and then <code>drinks_list</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Display each drink from <code>drinks_list</code> only once by converting the list.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"drinks_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;espresso&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;americano&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(set(drinks_list))\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"82\" endIndex=\"85\" /><option startIndex=\"85\" endIndex=\"86\" /><option startIndex=\"86\" endIndex=\"97\" /><option startIndex=\"97\" endIndex=\"98\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"list\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"tuple\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>set</code>, followed by <code>(</code>, <code>drinks_list</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          },
          {
            "title": "Example: Store in variable",
            "id": 89422,
            "contentType": "interactive",
            "images": [],
            "interactiveContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Create the variable <code>drinks_set</code> that stores the result of applying <code>set()</code> on <code>drinks_list</code>.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"drinks_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;espresso&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;americano&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"drinks_set = set(drinks_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(drinks_set)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"87\" /><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option startIndex=\"93\" endIndex=\"94\" /><option startIndex=\"94\" endIndex=\"105\" /><option startIndex=\"105\" endIndex=\"106\" /></options></interaction></interactions><output><content><text value=\"{'matcha', 'americano', 'chai', 'espresso'}\" /></content></output></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>drinks_set</code> followed by <code>=</code> and then <code>set</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>drinks_list</code>, <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeContent": "<!DOCTYPE html ><html><body><p>Store each drink from <code>drinks_list</code> only once in <code>drinks_set</code>, then display that set.</p><code version=\"2\" codelang=\"python\" name=\"script.py\" visible-if=\"always\"><content><text value=\"drinks_list = [\" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;espresso&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;americano&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;chai&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\", \" /><text value=\"&quot;matcha&quot;\" class=\"string\" /><text value=\"]\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"drinks_set = set(drinks_list)\" /><text type=\"break\" /><text value=\"print(drinks_set)\" /></content><interactions><interaction type=\"fillTheGap\" isDefault=\"true\"><options><option startIndex=\"77\" endIndex=\"87\" /><option startIndex=\"88\" endIndex=\"89\" /><option startIndex=\"90\" endIndex=\"93\" /><option startIndex=\"93\" endIndex=\"94\" /><option startIndex=\"94\" endIndex=\"105\" /><option startIndex=\"105\" endIndex=\"106\" /><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"list\" /></content></option><option correct=\"false\"><content><text value=\"tuple\" /></content></option></options></interaction></interactions></code><p visible-if=\"wrong\">Make sure to pick <code>drinks_set</code>, followed by <code>=</code>, <code>set</code>, <code>(</code>, <code>drinks_list</code>, and finally <code>)</code>.</p></body></html>",
            "hardModeSelected": true
          }
        ]
